207
00:17:15,827 --> 00:17:20,563
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example,

208
00:17:20,583 --> 00:17:28,525
jersey has epsilon-zero of 18 percent and eta of 0.85. Set the ratio to 1.30:

209
00:17:28,545 --> 00:17:31,007
what is the edge strain?

210
00:17:31,407 --> 00:17:31,619
Or,

211
00:17:31,639 --> 00:17:37,266
the upper looper's minimum transmission angle is 39 degrees and the lower

212
00:17:37,286 --> 00:17:38,581
looper's is 49.5.

213
00:17:38,601 --> 00:17:40,901
For the same resisting torque,

214
00:17:40,921 --> 00:17:45,774
roughly how many times larger is the upper looper's link force?

215
00:17:46,174 --> 00:17:51,939
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

216
00:17:53,459 --> 00:17:55,559
Three things to remember.

217
00:17:55,959 --> 00:18:03,384
One: in stitch 504 each of three threads has its own job, with no tight knot,

218
00:18:03,404 --> 00:18:08,605
so it stretches; each stitch needs three loop entries,

219
00:18:08,625 --> 00:18:12,859
at the right moment and with tiny clearance.

220
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:18,990
Two: the lower looper is driven by a spatial RSSR four-bar,

221
00:18:19,010 --> 00:18:25,910
analysed entirely from the constant link length, which gives the swing,

222
00:18:25,930 --> 00:18:29,516
angular speed and transmission angle.

223
00:18:29,916 --> 00:18:32,992
Three: differential feed,

224
00:18:33,012 --> 00:18:41,785
with flat-edge ratio 1 plus epsilon-zero over eta and wave height about

225
00:18:41,805 --> 00:18:45,252
lambda root epsilon over pi.

